- Manual findings:
  - PTBOCTL VDD_UBOR and VDDA_UBOR are the brown-out event-action fields.
  - PWRTC.VDD_UBOR and PWRTC.VDDA_UBOR are per-rail brown-out cause/status bits and the PWRTC register is RW1C, so writing those bits back to PWRTC is the correct clear path for the per-rail cause latches.
  - The combined BOR interrupt clear path remains SYSCTL_MISC.BOR, which matches the existing SYSCTL_InterruptSource.c implementation.
  - LDOSPCTL, LDOSPCAL, LDODPCTL, and LDODPCAL are documented in System Control Register 25 through Register 28 on pages 313 through 318 and the wrappers in SYSCTL_LDOVoltage.c are direct register-field wrappers.
- Additional consistency finding:
  - SYSCTL peripheral struct definitions for LDODPCAL label the fields inconsistently with the manual and the raw register macros; the deep-sleep calibration register should expose NOPLL and KHZ30, not WITHPLL.
- Decision:
  - keep SYSCTL_Voltage.c brown-out clear helpers intact
  - fix the real LDO production inconsistencies in the register-family definitions while adding focused host tests for SYSCTL_LDOVoltage.c and SYSCTL_Voltage.c.
